-- title:
--   Original intrinsic negative jump occupation equals the physical Lévy product under rightCont future source rectangles
-- statement:
--   For the literal intrinsic original path jump count NX, its lifted original-source occupation M=P.bind K, inclusive finite-horizon restriction MT, and physical rightCont predictable clock product N=μ×(X.ν restricted to negative marks), exact equality MT=N follows from (i) the original source zero-time atom bound transported by hμclock, (ii) separately supplied rightCont future-rectangle source intensity hFuture, and (iii) countable finite-mark-band σ-finite uniqueness. This isolates precisely the source-time transport needed by the controlled Itô–Meyer generator compensation. No generic predictable clock is asserted to be the source compensator.
-- source:
--   Wave6 Chat04 extraction from accepted original-source pathwise L1 proof candidate 21817; source-time transport lemma separated for Chat06 L2 and martingale consumers.

